<section class="walkthrough" aria-label="Inside Oore CI">
  <div class="story">
    <p class="small-label">WHY I BUILT IT</p>
    <h2>From my own release workflow.</h2>
    <p>I wanted to run Flutter mobile CI on my own Mac, handle signing, and share internal builds without stitching together too many tools. Oore started there.</p>
  </div>

  <figure>
    <figcaption>
      <p class="small-label">01 / The dashboard</p>
    <h2>A place to start the day.</h2>
    <p>The dashboard brings running builds, waiting jobs, and runner availability together. Problems surface alongside the work: here, a source that cannot be checked out needs attention before its build can start.</p>
    </figcaption>
    <a class="shot-light" href="/projects/oore-build/dashboard.webp" aria-label="Open the Oore dashboard screenshot at full size">
      <img src="/projects/oore-build/dashboard.webp" width="1440" height="900" alt="Oore dashboard showing running builds, the queue, runner availability, and a source error that needs attention." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </a>
    <a class="shot-dark" href="/projects/oore-build/dashboard-dark.webp" aria-label="Open the Oore dashboard screenshot at full size">
      <img src="/projects/oore-build/dashboard-dark.webp" width="1440" height="900" alt="Oore dashboard showing running builds, the queue, runner availability, and a source error that needs attention." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </a>
    <p class="image-note">Real product UI · Demo data · Tap to enlarge</p>
  </figure>

  <figure>
    <figcaption>
      <p class="small-label">02 / The build queue</p>
    <h2>From a commit to a build.</h2>
    <p>Each run keeps its project, branch, commit, and trigger together. Filter by project or status to find a release, or see what is still queued. GitHub and GitLab webhooks can start builds when code changes.</p>
    </figcaption>
    <a class="shot-light" href="/projects/oore-build/builds.webp" aria-label="Open the Oore builds screenshot at full size">
      <img src="/projects/oore-build/builds.webp" width="1440" height="900" alt="Oore builds list with projects, queued and running jobs, completed builds, branches, commits, and build triggers." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </a>
    <a class="shot-dark" href="/projects/oore-build/builds-dark.webp" aria-label="Open the Oore builds screenshot at full size">
      <img src="/projects/oore-build/builds-dark.webp" width="1440" height="900" alt="Oore builds list with projects, queued and running jobs, completed builds, branches, commits, and build triggers." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </a>
    <p class="image-note">Real product UI · Demo data · Tap to enlarge</p>
  </figure>

  <div class="closing">
    <div>
      <p class="small-label">AFTER THE BUILD</p>
      <h3>Share what you made.</h3>
      <p>Oore also handles signing workflows and artifact delivery through signed, time-limited links. Android, iOS, and macOS Flutter builds run on your own macOS infrastructure.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="small-label">THE TRADEOFF</p>
      <h3>Your machine, your upkeep.</h3>
      <p>Self-hosting means keeping the build machine and toolchain running yourself. Oore is still in public alpha, with room to improve through real use and feedback.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <a class="grid-button" href="/blog/oore-build-public-alpha">Read the public alpha story ↗</a>
</section>

